{"availability":"available","full":"phuanh20001/Muster-POS","name":"Muster-POS","description":"Full-stack point-of-sale for a coffee shop. Next.js 16, Prisma, PostgreSQL, three card processors behind one interface (Stripe, Square Terminal, Linkly EFTPOS), decimal-safe money, offline PWA tills. Live demo included.","category":"Finance","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-31T05:05:18Z","updated":"2026-09-15T12:39:13Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://dreamy-cafe.vercel.app","topics":["fullstack","nextjs","payments","point-of-sale","postgresql","prisma","pwa","react","square","stripe"],"demo":"https://dreamy-cafe.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:17.975Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:17.975Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:17.975Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:42:17.975Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A production point-of-sale and online-ordering system for a coffee shop, built to actually run a real till, print real dockets, and take real card payments over the counter and online.","Linkly accredited for on-premises bank EFTPOS (TCPIP OnPrem, September 2026) and listed on Linkly’s public Accredited POS directory. Linkly is the middleware behind most Australian bank EFTPOS terminals, and driving one from your own software requires passing their test suite, including the mandatory power-failure and recovery cases. The integration runs in production, but its source is kept private and is not part of this snapshot. I’m happy to walk through it in an interview.","Most POS side-projects stop at \"add item to cart, fake a checkout.\" The interesting engineering here is in the parts that are easy to get subtly wrong and expensive to get wrong in production. Four decisions do most of the heavy lifting:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e26d7b53b5264e48dedc38b3cac58c8ae42d7c6a13b77eaa9324f995b39d7335","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:18.057Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:18.057Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A production point-of-sale and online-ordering system for a coffee shop, built to actually run a real till, print real dockets, and take real card payments over the counter and online.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"It runs self-hosted on the shop's own PC, with only the customer-facing routes exposed to the internet.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"POS — cart, modifiers/add-ons, sizes, combos, tables & floor plan, split-by-price or split-by-product, surcharges, discounts; staff PIN login","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Three roles, two back-office panels with separate login cookies (a deliberate decoupling — the Owner PIN alone grants /admin/ without a prior Manager login):","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Self-hosted on the shop PC: the app + local PostgreSQL run on the trusted LAN, and only customer routes (/, /order, /onlineorder, /loyalty) are exposed to the internet via a Cloudflare Tunnel.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e26d7b53b5264e48dedc38b3cac58c8ae42d7c6a13b77eaa9324f995b39d7335","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T05:42:18.057Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-15T12:39:13Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/phuanh20001/Muster-POS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10